---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Quality & Test Reports | ISO 9001-Certified Production"
  description="Our quality system and test reports for tower packing and internals: dimensional, mechanical, material and chemical resistance testing. ISO 9001-certified production."
  canonical="https://www.mass-transfer.com/quality/"
  breadcrumb={[{ label: 'Quality & Tests' }]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="page-title">Quality &amp; Test Reports</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">
      Consistent quality is the whole point of buying from a certified supplier. Here is how we verify every batch before it ships.
    </p>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Quality System</h2>
      <p>
        Production runs under an <strong>ISO 9001-certified</strong> quality management system, covering incoming material, in-process control and final inspection.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Test</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dimensions</strong> — nominal size, wall thickness and geometry against specification.</li>
        <li><strong>Mechanical strength</strong> — crush and load tests to confirm the bed will carry its design load.</li>
        <li><strong>Material composition</strong> — alloy and polymer verification to confirm you receive the grade you ordered.</li>
        <li><strong>Chemical resistance</strong> — acid/alkali resistance testing for ceramic and plastic grades where relevant.</li>
        <li><strong>Surface quality</strong> — visual inspection for burrs, cracks and defects.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Documentation You Receive</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Inspection report per batch</li>
        <li>Material certificate where applicable</li>
        <li>Packing and loading photos</li>
        <li>Shipment documents and marks</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Need a specific test or certificate for your project? Tell us the standard — we confirm what we can supply before you commit.
      </p>
    </article>

    <Cta heading="Request sample inspection reports" />
  </div>
</Layout>
